# `on change b + c {…}`: the block runs when a write changed the expression's value
'b = 1; c = 2; n = 0; on change b + c { n += 1 }; b = 5; n'	1
'b = 1; c = 2; n = 0; on change b + c { n += 1 }; b = 5; c = 2; b = 5; n'	1
'b = 1; c = 2; n = 0; on change b * c { n += 1 }; b = 5; c = 3; n'	2
# a test line after a listener, the program's last, is tested where it stands
'b = 1; on change b { print 1 }; test b == 1'	ø
'b = 1; n = 0; on change b { n += 1 }; b = 2; n'	1
# a `:=` value is a derived signal: on change runs after a write changed its value (wiki/signal.md, card playground-tour)
'price = 3; count = 2; total := price * count; seen = 0; on change total { seen = value }; count = 5; seen'	15
